    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance that is visible from both directions of approach.\n• Mark the detached structure with a separate address or unit identifier so responders can quickly distinguish it from the main residence.\n• Clear vegetation along both sides of the access drive to allow emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Trim any trees or shrubs overhanging the access drive to maintain vertical clearance for fire apparatus and ladder trucks.\n• Keep the access drive surface clear of parked vehicles, stored equipment, and debris to allow a responding vehicle to reach both structures without stopping.\n• Designate and mark a turnaround area near the end of the access drive so responding vehicles are not required to back out onto the road.\n• Keep a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings on foot.\n• Store equipment and materials inside the equipment storage area rather than in front of or beside it, so the surrounding ground remains clear for responder movement.\n• Keep the storage areas clear of stacked materials that would block access to the sides or rear of either structure.\n• Post a simple site diagram at the driveway entrance showing the location of both structures, the storage areas, and the access drive layout."
